{"title":"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Alcumus)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Alcumus)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle is centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is a diameter and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is a point on the circle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/c/84c88bb622b5ba9f7b6a3673f5678d7f07d411de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle COB = 50^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" />. What is the degree measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39a4406ab9a6a9f1d35009c2e18008d1888fc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAB$\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/0/db0a17d52f373a09a58a20a602ead4ff89315cf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 20 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 25 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 45 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 50 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 65$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Assuming we do not already know an inscribed angle is always half of its central angle, we will try a different approach. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the center, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f8f2f1a3ddc6b42fae25a0637e85c747875180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a762ac8b4e23ffdd778ad6d5a8b97df8c7ce01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> are radii and they are congruent. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/2/0e2d97829369bc06782c17988a22533979294d85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle COA$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is an isosceles triangle. Also, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/d/e2d87c2746bf18130f641d2c6b17a0fa902f7863.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle COB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/f/3cf72d4dd6847fd821094c422f8dcbde99783d5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle COA$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> are supplementary, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/d/c0d83016880958075b6f571c7adb6da7c2bc0bfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle COA = 180 - 50 = 130^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"204\" height=\"13\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/2/0e2d97829369bc06782c17988a22533979294d85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle COA$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is isosceles, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c7054cee947c8430936a8e15679fdfc6f0be120.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OCA \\cong \\angle OAC$\" width=\"134\" height=\"13\" />. They also sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/c/5ec5fcabc29d46f91b1f4f628000fa40148d30a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />, so each angle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/e/16ee3ac3feaf0a603a95b83293fadb2847fb639a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Alcumus.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Alcumus)\">Solution 2 (Alcumus)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Alcumus)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/0/390aeef54428ca10528507b040ce5ee80640cb8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AOC = 180^\\circ - 50^\\circ = 130^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"219\" height=\"13\" />. Because triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/2/0129518bfc1d0df50eeb37d3d6a62b0a0327a85e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AOC$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is isosceles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/b/4bb5c04464d10b458f7578ee6da5c83ea8efb289.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAB = (180^\\circ - 130^\\circ)/2 = \\boxed{25^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"266\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/b/aab4fe9f0a401fcda884f1328c442a93c5cf59bb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph;  unitsize(2 cm);  pair O, A, B, C;  O = (0,0); A = (-1,0); B = (1,0); C = dir(50);  draw(Circle(O,1)); draw(B--A--C--O);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, W); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, E); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, NE); label(&quot;$O$&quot;, O, S); [/asy]\" width=\"238\" height=\"192\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/wqRMJBoSm_A\">https://youtu.be/wqRMJBoSm_A</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/I3yihAO87CE\">https://youtu.be/I3yihAO87CE</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B\">2010 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <